{"duration_api_ms":845692,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"b3582635-083d-4d21-a877-4ec6aedfc636","total_cost_usd":27.8456845,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11482,"cache_read_input_tokens":2053597,"output_tokens":2563,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":392},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11482,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1184,"cache_read_input_tokens":414201,"cache_creation_input_tokens":920,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":920},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5[1m]":{"inputTokens":300,"outputTokens":79335,"thinkingTokens":23155,"cacheReadInputTokens":43544199,"cacheCreationInputTokens":408871,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":27.8456845,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":6,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"The Linux desktop entry now accepts files: `Exec=librepili %U` instead of `%u`. It also advertises nine video MIME types, one for each extension in `LocalPlayer.videoExtensions`: mp4, mkv, webm, mov, m4v, flv, avi, ts and wmv. The `bilibili` scheme handler is unchanged. This is not tested on Linux.\n\nI checked everything that installs or references the file, and none of it needed changing:\n- **deb:** `linux_x64.yml:63` copies the file as is, and `DEBIAN/postinst` / `postrm` already run `update-desktop-database`, so the new MIME types get registered.\n- **rpm:** lines 105 and 138 install the file unchanged, and the `%post` / `%postun` steps (144, 148) also run `update-desktop-database`.\n- **AppImage:** lines 190–191 copy the file. The two `sed` lines at 207–208 replace text with itself, so they have no effect on `%U`.\n\nOne behaviour to know about: file managers usually pass a `file://` URI rather than a plain path. `main()` doesn't recognise a URI at launch, so the file is opened by the link-stream handler I added last round, which converts `file:` URIs to paths. It still opens once either way. With several files selected, only the first is opened.\n\n```diff\ndiff --git a/assets/linux/com.zxa24.librepili.desktop b/assets/linux/com.zxa24.librepili.desktop\nindex df48d7e94..f70fb7593 100644\n--- a/assets/linux/com.zxa24.librepili.desktop\n+++ b/assets/linux/com.zxa24.librepili.desktop\n@@ -3,9 +3,9 @@ Type=Application\n Name=LibrePili\n Comment=A third-party Bilibili Client developed in Flutter\n Comment[zh_CN]=使用 Flutter 开发的 BiliBili 第三方客户端\n-Exec=librepili %u\n+Exec=librepili %U\n Icon=librepili\n Terminal=false\n StartupWMClass=com.zxa24.librepili\n Categories=Video;AudioVideo;Player;\n-MimeType=x-scheme-handler/bilibili;\n+MimeType=x-scheme-handler/bilibili;video/mp4;video/x-matroska;video/webm;video/quicktime;video/x-m4v;video/x-flv;video/x-msvideo;video/mp2t;video/x-ms-wmv;\n```\n\n`dart analyze lib test` still shows 0 errors and 0 warnings (36 info-level lints, all pre-existing).\n\n```\nTEST RESULTS:\n  runner: flutter test (+ dart analyze lib test)\n  command: source \".../scratchpad/tools/local_env.sh\" && cd \"$REPO\" && dart analyze lib test && flutter test\n  exit_code: 0\n  total: 62\n  passed: 62\n  failed: 0\n  skipped: 0\n  duration_ms: ~41000 (analyze + test)\n\nINFRA REPAIRS (during auto-repair, empty if none):\n\nREAL FAILURES (audit-fix-caused regressions, empty if none):\n\nINFRA-PERSISTENT (failures that hit the 3-cycle repair cap, empty if none):\n\nOVERALL: PASS\n```\n\nThe Gmail, Google Calendar and Google Drive connectors still need authorizing in claude.ai connector settings, and the `agentbridge` server still fails to connect. Neither was needed here.","ttft_ms":5163,"type":"result","duration_ms":78239,"uuid":"94737a1e-5543-4221-a311-6e5f6ded5f2f","ttft_stream_ms":2997,"time_to_request_ms":447,"first_content_frame_ms":2998,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":1}
